From 7cac8c4f7c34293eec6d44175d96f9f9e3df9a2f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sm64ds-3ds <244728604+ethanseagull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:45:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hal: engine A's full 2D boards composed in a fraction of the
 time

A minigame's top screen is three or four whole text BGs, and composing it took 25-77 ms of a frame on the 3DS. Now: the BGs are kept as whole-map pictures that redraw only changed tiles; a whole visible run of a layer that can't blend goes straight in; a native scene's cells go out in rows without the per-cell decisions (and without the HUD element labels it never uses); the pause-menu memo backs off on a screen that keeps changing. The cells match the reference loop (SM64DS_TWOD_VERIFY=1: minigames, title, intro, levels 1 and 6, the pause menu, the touch menus).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 port/hal/message_compositor.cpp | 362 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 353 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/port/hal/message_compositor.cpp b/port/hal/message_compositor.cpp
